WEBVTT

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:26.660
The quaint village of Sugar Creek is nestled in the rolling hills of Tuscarora County.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:38.620
The Ohio Central Locomotive, stationed downtown Sugar Creek, takes you six miles into the heart of Amish farmland.

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:41.560
A round trip takes just about an hour.

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:50.460
Across from the station is Dale's Blacksmith Shop, where the Amish bring their farm horses and carriage horses to be shooed.

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:56.790
A buggy horse needs horseshoes to protect its feet from hard surfaced roads.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:59.400
Horseshoes are made of iron.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.600
and are pounded by the blacksmith to perfectly fit the shape of the horse's hoop.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:37.860
A blacksmith is an artisan who shapes and welds iron to produce horseshoes and other tools or utensils made of iron.

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:41.940
The iron horseshoe must be heated until it's red hot.

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:49.880
It is then placed on the anvil where it is hammered into the desired shape so as to create a perfect fit.

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:42.000
Horses' hooves grow like human fingernails, so the horses need to be refitted on average every 10 weeks.

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:15.270
Nails are positioned so they protrude through the edge of the horse's hoop.

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:22.060
The points are clenched, which holds the shoe on tightly and prevents it from vibrating loose.

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:26.420
Nailing the shoes on in no way hurts the horse.

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:29.970
In fact, horses become accustomed to having their...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.280
who's manicured.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:09.050
All right.

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:34.430
Oh

00:13:07.610 --> 00:13:09.230
We're the nerve-ending stuff.

00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:18.140
On the bottom, which is just simply going too short, that's about it.

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:21.860
But they've got a wall around the outside you can be able to.

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:27.740
Since the development of automobiles, the number of blacksmiths has been greatly reduced.

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:29.980
Fortunately for the Amish of Sugar...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:35.720
Creek and surrounding areas, Dale's blacksmith shop has kept this unique art

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:44.740
alive. The town of Sugar Creek is known throughout Ohio as Little Switzerland. The

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:49.020
town was settled by immigrants from Switzerland and the Swiss styling is

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:58.170
apparent throughout the town. Sugar Creek is located amidst the largest

00:13:58.170 --> 00:13:59.530
Amish community in the world.

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:03.630
It is quite common to see horse-drawn buggies on their streets,

00:14:03.930 --> 00:14:08.370
parked near the shops, the general store, and of course, the blacksmith shop.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:18.560
As you wander around the town of Sugar Creek,

00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:23.040
you'll quickly notice unique murals on many of the buildings,

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:25.260
many of which are animated.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:29.550
Few have been more responsible for transforming...

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:39.910
Sugar Creek into the little Switzerland of Ohio than artist Tom Miller. He has painted dozens of

00:14:39.910 --> 00:14:47.220
murals with Swiss scenes and Amish country landscapes throughout the town. Be sure and

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:53.300
visit his gallery while in Sugar Creek. It showcases both original paintings, prints, and

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:58.900
drawings. Some of them date back over 50 years from when Tom began his artistic career.

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:05.390
Let's peek inside his studio and watch Tom at work on one of his favorite themes,

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:07.360
the life of Christ.

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:16.210
For over 60 years, Tom has put paint to canvas, wood, and board.

00:15:17.210 --> 00:15:24.130
Tom's creative talents include paintings with oils, pastels, charcoal, and acrylics.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:29.970
As a tribute to Tom Miller's vision, contribution, and talent,

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:38.470
the Sugar Creek Business Association has honored him with the Tom Miller Sugar Creek Arts Festival

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:48.440
every May for the last four years. This festival features an auction of 10 to 20 of Tom's finest paintings

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:52.320
and prints that he created over the past year.

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:08.740
This was the top set of last year, and this is the premier where you can get a thousand

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:09.200
audits.

00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:39.050
Here's the proud owner of one of Tom's latest originals.

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:46.150
The festival also features an arts and crafts street fair,

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:51.590
where 50 to 60 artisans and crafters feature their wares.

00:16:57.840 --> 00:16:59.980
One of Ohio's largest festivals is...

00:17:00.030 --> 00:17:05.530
the Ohio Swiss Festival held each year in Sugar Creek. Almost a quarter of a

00:17:05.530 --> 00:17:09.850
million people swarm into the town to enjoy the food, entertainment, and parade.

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:15.800
There are lots of creative events scheduled such as the stein tossing or

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:20.840
stone toss, yodeling, and the Swiss style wrestling all add to the fun.

00:17:31.560 --> 00:17:35.060
The Swiss Parade is a perfect example of small-town America.

00:17:35.060 --> 00:17:43.320
It features marching high school bands, classic cars, unique floats, and lots of horse-drawn buggies and carriages.

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:56.880
When a horse is such an integral part of the Amish lifestyle, no other animal is as important and well cared for.

00:18:58.040 --> 00:18:59.960
When the Amish want to buy...

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:16.450
or sell one of their work horses or carriage horses they head for the auction one of the first

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:22.460
buildings we pass going out of town is the sugar creek horse auction building where every week

00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:29.850
farmers and country folk come from miles around to buy and sell their horses i'd guess 50 percent of

00:19:30.090 --> 00:19:32.230
in attendance are simply there for the show.

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:44.780
Amish-made quilts are a major attraction for many visiting this area.

00:20:45.740 --> 00:20:51.540
The Swiss Village Quilts and Craft Shop is a great place to browse and gain an understanding

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:56.820
of just how much labor goes into making one of these handmade quilts.

00:20:57.500 --> 00:20:59.820
Quilt-making is a primary means of art.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:03.580
artistic expression and income for many Amish women.

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:08.560
The artistic style of any given quilt is determined well

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:13.700
before the quilt is sewn together. Colors, quilt size,

00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:17.570
symmetry, and layout all must be properly

00:21:17.570 --> 00:21:22.280
planned. A variety of unique patterns must be cut out from

00:21:22.370 --> 00:21:26.530
material scraps in the shapes of bars, squares,

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:29.830
diamonds, rectangles, triangles, and petals.

00:21:30.320 --> 00:21:38.640
all coming together to form one of these unique creations artisans mercantile and beachy chalet

00:21:38.640 --> 00:21:44.380
restaurant are located just across the tracks from downtown sugar creek and are two other great

00:21:44.380 --> 00:21:51.660
places to shop or browse for quilts both offer a large selection of very unique quilts and amish

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:58.860
made woodwork the amish are well-respected craftsmen their country style woodwork is both comfortable

00:21:58.860 --> 00:21:59.660
and

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:09.430
distinctive. An investment in any of these fine quilts or furnishings is sure to become a family heirloom.

00:22:13.980 --> 00:22:25.790
In some areas of Ohio's Amish country, you can drive for miles and miles and see nothing but Amish farms, green pastures, and fields of whispering wheat.

00:23:16.280 --> 00:23:23.660
Backroads is always an adventure filled with relaxing scenery and sometimes unique surprises

00:23:23.660 --> 00:23:29.720
like last spring when I encountered what I refer to as an Amish house moving.

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:38.710
Since built in 1869, this home was the pioneer homestead of Sugar Creek, owned by John S.

00:23:38.830 --> 00:23:46.500
Yoder, where he and his family lived and farmed their 100-acre tract of land, a tract now

00:23:46.500 --> 00:23:48.660
known as the town of Sugar Creek.

00:23:49.420 --> 00:23:55.850
The Amish Heritage Foundation was formed to preserve this historic home, moving the house

00:23:55.850 --> 00:23:59.790
from its historic location to a field approximately a mile away.

00:24:00.340 --> 00:24:03.700
proved to be a timely and expensive undertaking.

00:24:04.140 --> 00:24:09.830
Moving the house over the grass yard onto the street is literally an inch-by-inch process.

00:24:10.210 --> 00:24:14.970
Strong planks are placed under the rear wheels to disperse the...

00:24:15.030 --> 00:24:23.020
huge 75 tons of weight and prevent damage from the tires. Watch and appreciate the tremendous

00:24:23.020 --> 00:24:27.640
effort and group cooperation that goes into this massive task.

00:24:30.988 --> 00:24:32.988
You

00:28:42.160 --> 00:28:47.250
satisfied with mere diesel power, a local Amish farmer hooks up his team of

00:28:47.250 --> 00:28:49.460
Belgians for a little added horsepower.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:05.840
That is what the truck is doing.

00:29:20.380 --> 00:29:21.980
151,500.

00:29:38.190 --> 00:29:50.680
Thanks to the collective efforts of six men, Dave Beachy, Emanuel Schrock, Roman Yoder, Noah Troyer, Tim Yoder, Henry Schrock, and Blaine Miller,

00:29:51.230 --> 00:29:59.700
the original farmhouse of Sugar Creek now rests on a donated one-acre tract of land awaiting complete restoration.

00:30:00.820 --> 00:30:08.420
Coincidentally, the tract of land that this house now rests on once belonged to John S. Yoder's family.

00:30:12.630 --> 00:30:17.790
Amish children are treasured and loved and nurtured throughout their childhood.

00:30:18.390 --> 00:30:25.290
These children have an innocence and naturalness that directly reflects their basic and simple lifestyle.

00:30:31.280 --> 00:30:39.680
The Amish have their own schools because they want to give their children teachings that they will need to earn an honest living and to lead a Christian life.

00:30:40.590 --> 00:30:44.830
A special focus is made on teaching respect and responsibility.

00:30:47.110 --> 00:30:49.850
The favorite sport of Amish children is baseball.

00:30:50.420 --> 00:30:55.620
It's virtually impossible to drive by an Amish schoolhouse without a baseball diamond.

00:30:56.180 --> 00:30:59.480
And if you catch them during recess or after school,

00:31:00.510 --> 00:31:11.450
likely to catch a game in progress. Notice here that some of the boys are wearing baseball gloves.

00:31:12.510 --> 00:31:19.190
Some Amish school boards forbid the use of baseball gloves and hard baseballs while playing

00:31:19.190 --> 00:31:26.580
baseball at school. They believe a sponge ball or other softball prevents the game from becoming

00:31:26.580 --> 00:31:29.980
too competitive with worldly methods and goals.

00:31:30.220 --> 00:31:36.120
which might range out of control among teenagers and be carried on into adulthood.

00:31:37.240 --> 00:31:40.960
Amish children go to school for eight years through the eighth grade.

00:31:41.650 --> 00:31:45.550
There is one teacher, and all eight grades are taught under one roof.

00:31:59.010 --> 00:31:59.970
Amish children have...

00:32:00.060 --> 00:32:06.760
lots of playmates. Their large families provide plenty of brothers and sisters, plus lots of

00:32:06.760 --> 00:32:20.010
cousins and neighbors. Domish children come home from school. They first help around the home with

00:32:20.010 --> 00:32:25.640
chores, and they love to go to the market with mom or dad to socialize with friends and neighbors.

00:32:35.400 --> 00:32:41.980
Amish boys begin riding along with Dad on his horse-drawn farming implements at a very young age

00:32:42.160 --> 00:32:46.580
and begin helping with farming chores as soon as they are able.

00:33:21.440 --> 00:33:27.560
seems to be crumbling in North America, the Amish make every effort possible to

00:33:27.560 --> 00:33:29.360
preserve their family lifestyle.

00:33:30.960 --> 00:33:37.580
What the outside world may judge as radical, non-conformist practices of Amish life,

00:33:38.100 --> 00:33:45.640
the Amish have deliberately instituted such an austere lifestyle to nurture family cohesiveness.

00:33:46.330 --> 00:33:55.600
Thus, the horse-drawn buggy, easy, fast transportation, draws family members too far away from home.

00:34:27.450 --> 00:34:28.370
and develop other interests.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:35.890
Play among children in the Amish community cultivates more creativity and less competition.

00:34:36.890 --> 00:34:44.480
Most Amish people are living proof that it's possible to have fun without television, video games, and computers.

00:34:56.140 --> 00:34:59.980
Amish toys are also unique and stick to the plain and simple...

00:35:01.400 --> 00:35:09.590
Let's visit an Amish toy and craftmaker's workshop and watch as he makes fun yet simple toys, furniture, and games.

00:36:45.830 --> 00:36:50.030
Observer that Amish children delight in their country living lifestyle.

00:36:50.960 --> 00:36:58.820
Little boys have time to fish and explore nature, while little girls play with their sisters, cousins, schoolmates, and neighbors.

00:37:37.390 --> 00:37:44.380
Travel by horse-drawn buggy is both scenic and relaxing, that is, if all goes well.

00:38:00.700 --> 00:38:08.540
buggy riding on rural roads is not without risk cars trucks and semi-trailers all pose grave

00:38:08.540 --> 00:38:14.400
risks when suddenly encountered with a horse-drawn buggy traveling five miles an hour or less

00:38:19.510 --> 00:38:24.520
ohio's amish country is very hilly it was this terrain that attracted them

00:38:24.760 --> 00:38:29.810
reminiscent of their motherlands terrain, but their motherlands didn't have

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:59.980
tractor trailers and motorhomes and trucks. I highly advise visit...

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:06.650
to this area to use extra caution, especially when traveling around curves and over hills.

00:39:07.500 --> 00:39:14.250
And if you ever have a chance to slow down or stop as to help a buggy cross an intersection,

00:39:14.720 --> 00:39:19.490
one that obviously needs a traffic light but has none, please do so.

00:39:20.980 --> 00:39:27.230
The Amish enjoy tourism. A great deal of them are employed as a direct result of the tourist trade.

00:39:27.230 --> 00:39:29.610
by the same token.

00:39:30.160 --> 00:39:38.580
I respect the plight of the Amish when it comes to having to confront a car from the perspective of driving a horse-drawn buggy.

00:39:47.730 --> 00:39:54.430
There are a few buggy tours that will take you several miles deep into the back roads that make this area so scenic.

00:39:55.060 --> 00:39:59.600
And even on these quiet back roads, people speed by buggies.

00:40:00.280 --> 00:40:07.440
cut in dangerously close after passing, every other day an accident occurs involving a horse-drawn

00:40:07.440 --> 00:40:20.680
buggy and a car, RV, truck, or semi. Watching a scene like this takes me back to a way of life I

00:40:20.680 --> 00:40:27.520
know my ancestors knew. How fortunate we are to have the Amish to remind us that plain and simple

00:40:27.520 --> 00:40:29.410
can be far less stressful.

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:33.340
and just as rewarding than ornate and complex.

00:40:39.140 --> 00:40:41.180
The average speed of a horse-drawn buggy

00:40:41.180 --> 00:40:42.660
is about eight miles per hour.

00:40:43.280 --> 00:40:46.260
Faster speeds are possible for short distances,

00:40:46.800 --> 00:40:49.820
but are discouraged unless it's an emergency.

00:40:50.620 --> 00:40:54.600
A good horse can travel for about 20 miles without stopping,

00:40:55.050 --> 00:40:57.510
but then needs to rest for several hours.

00:41:16.320 --> 00:41:21.640
For longer trips, two horses will be hitched to the carriage, reducing the workload in half.

00:41:22.520 --> 00:41:26.960
Nearly all buggy horses are animals that were once used for harness racing.

00:41:27.400 --> 00:41:29.960
If a horse isn't quite fast enough to...

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:35.680
race competitively, they quickly end up at one of the three major horse auctions in this area.

00:41:37.190 --> 00:41:44.140
Seeing Amish country by buggy gives one a deeper perspective and appreciation for what this unique

00:41:44.140 --> 00:41:51.000
slice of Americana is all about. The Amish deliberately choose their life of austerity.

00:41:51.780 --> 00:41:59.810
Amish simplicity is indivisible. You cannot analyze it or dissect it. Simplicity for simplicity

00:42:00.090 --> 00:42:06.710
sake is difficult for some to understand. That's why so much that is simple evades knowledge.

00:42:07.690 --> 00:42:15.200
God's presence is simple, yet God evades science. The complex scientific mind does not know God.

00:42:16.130 --> 00:42:23.000
Love is simple, yet science does not know love. To understand simplicity, you have to drop the

00:42:23.000 --> 00:42:29.320
desire and effort to understand it rationally. Only then can you understand it.

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:35.880
A new kind of understanding is needed, an understanding of the heart and not the mind

00:42:35.880 --> 00:42:43.300
will be necessary, an understanding that does not analyze, dissect, and rationalize.

00:42:44.090 --> 00:42:51.180
Simplicity means to be in deep communion with God, oneself, family, and your neighbor.

00:42:51.920 --> 00:42:58.340
To be perfectly comfortable living your life in your own way, a way that you find brings

00:42:58.340 --> 00:42:59.480
you closer to God.

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:29.120
and creation itself. Amish boys and girls are taught how to ride a buggy on country backroads

00:43:29.120 --> 00:43:29.980
at a very young age.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:36.120
usually around nine years old. Young teenage boys will receive their first

00:43:36.120 --> 00:43:59.870
buggy by the time they're age 16. Exploring the back

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:06.330
roads of Amish country is very relaxing. If you have a chance to see it by buggy, don't pass it up.

00:44:06.990 --> 00:44:17.100
Just sit back and relax and listen to the clip-clop of the horse's hooves. As we continue our

00:44:17.100 --> 00:44:22.670
journey through Amish country, I'd like to tell you some important and interesting points concerning

00:44:22.670 --> 00:44:28.860
the Amish way of life. So we'll hop back aboard the Ohio Central and take a closer look at some

00:44:28.860 --> 00:44:29.980
Amish farmsteads.

00:45:23.320 --> 00:45:28.390
When traveling past Amish farmsteads, you'll often notice that there are two houses built

00:45:28.390 --> 00:45:29.470
side by side.

00:45:30.090 --> 00:45:32.690
or a smaller house attached to the main house.

00:45:33.470 --> 00:45:35.890
The smaller house is known as the dowdy house.

00:45:36.930 --> 00:45:38.210
This is grandpa's house.

00:45:38.860 --> 00:45:40.740
After the parents surrender the farm

00:45:40.740 --> 00:45:42.760
to one of their eldest children,

00:45:43.510 --> 00:45:45.630
the dowdy house is built for the grandparents

00:45:45.630 --> 00:45:48.530
where they will be cared for for the rest of their years.

00:45:49.300 --> 00:45:52.060
The Amish believe in the children caring for the elderly

00:45:52.060 --> 00:45:53.820
and the grandparents are loved

00:45:53.820 --> 00:45:56.140
and appreciated forever in an Amish home.

00:46:01.080 --> 00:46:03.480
The size of an Amish farm varies greatly.

00:46:03.920 --> 00:46:08.440
It takes about 50 acres to sustain a family and work animals.

00:46:09.450 --> 00:46:14.680
Most farms in central Ohio's tri-county area average about 100 acres,

00:46:15.120 --> 00:46:18.900
double the size of a Lancaster, Pennsylvania Amish farm.

00:46:19.390 --> 00:46:23.660
But because this land is so hilly, you sometimes need 100 acres

00:46:23.660 --> 00:46:26.040
in order to have 50 acres that are tillable.

00:46:27.090 --> 00:46:29.750
The Amish are known as some of the world's best farmers.

00:46:30.570 --> 00:46:33.390
They're drawn to the land by their love for it.

00:46:34.000 --> 00:46:39.090
The Amish possess a profound sense of stewardship to care for God's good earth.

00:46:39.940 --> 00:46:44.520
They also believe that farm work is a healthy and satisfying way of life.

00:46:45.250 --> 00:46:51.250
They produce plentiful crops by investing long hours in careful planning of their crops.

00:47:02.940 --> 00:47:10.460
Crops always include both field corn and sweet corn, barley, alfalfa, and oats.

00:47:11.240 --> 00:47:16.640
Most of the land that is farmed is to raise crops to feed the farm animals.

00:47:18.590 --> 00:47:23.930
Belgian and Percheron horses are used to pull their antique-looking farming implements.

00:47:25.040 --> 00:47:29.980
Steel-wheeled tractors are used only for belt power to thresh or fill...

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:38.400
silos. Most of these horse-drawn farm machines are so old, not only are they no longer manufactured,

00:47:38.930 --> 00:47:47.410
but special parts must be made so they can fix or rebuild them year after year. Due to a limited

00:47:47.410 --> 00:47:54.360
supply of farmland, and the average Amish family has eight children, farming is only possible for

00:47:54.360 --> 00:47:59.940
a select few fortunate enough to inherit land from their family or are able to

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:07.090
buy a farm that occasionally goes up for sale by a non-Amish farmer. Many Amish

00:48:07.090 --> 00:48:12.480
families are involved with cottage industries. Like farming, these work-at-home

00:48:12.480 --> 00:48:17.180
businesses keep the family close and working together. Many of these

00:48:17.180 --> 00:48:22.890
businesses cater to the unique needs of the Amish community. Blacksmith shops,

00:48:23.130 --> 00:48:28.190
welding, harness repair, buggy manufacturing, and quilting all generate

00:48:28.190 --> 00:48:29.770
revenues that help sustain

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:35.840
their country living lifestyle. More and more Amish are catering to the English

00:48:35.840 --> 00:48:42.320
community. English are what the Amish call anyone that's not Amish. Today the

00:48:42.320 --> 00:48:47.420
Amish are heavily involved in building, cabinet and furniture making, catering

00:48:47.420 --> 00:48:52.510
and cooking, plus a variety of other services that cater to the tourist and

00:48:52.510 --> 00:48:53.170
English community.

00:49:00.120 --> 00:49:04.800
Most of us would think it impossible to live without electricity in today's world.

00:49:05.440 --> 00:49:09.810
The most basic of life's functions revolves around electricity.

00:49:10.260 --> 00:49:13.800
Lighting, heating, cooking, TV, and VCRs.

00:49:14.010 --> 00:49:15.850
They all depend upon electricity.

00:49:18.190 --> 00:49:26.070
But if you think about it, most rural Americans had no access to electricity until the 1930s or 40s.

00:49:26.520 --> 00:49:29.780
Many people who were alive during the first third of this century...

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:33.430
will be able to understand how the Amish live without electricity.

00:49:34.000 --> 00:49:37.680
In fact, to millions of people living in the third world nations,

00:49:38.190 --> 00:49:40.830
the Amish way of life would seem quite modern.

00:49:57.680 --> 00:49:59.980
A large portion of farms in this area...

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:07.910
are dairy farms. The milk check is an important part of the Amish farmer's income. Most Amish

00:50:07.910 --> 00:50:13.920
dairy farmers do all of their milking by hand. This requires help from the entire family.

00:50:14.870 --> 00:50:20.870
Every family member who is able will milk several cows twice a day, early morning and

00:50:20.870 --> 00:50:25.250
evening. The larger the family, usually the larger the herd of cows.

00:50:30.350 --> 00:50:36.870
I love dairy cows and often stop my car along the side of the country road and walk over the fence and call them.

00:50:37.720 --> 00:50:41.060
Quite often they'll come up and give you very unusual looks.

00:50:45.040 --> 00:50:49.060
Old order Amish still store milk in the old style milk can.

00:50:50.050 --> 00:50:54.810
These milk cans are then cooled by placing them in troughs of flowing water.

00:50:55.900 --> 00:50:59.960
Buyers of grade A milk require that the milk be refrigerated at least.

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:06.880
lower temperatures than are possible with this form of water cooling. So Amish dairy farmers

00:51:06.880 --> 00:51:13.130
who insist on only cooling their milk using the water method must sell their milk to cheese

00:51:13.130 --> 00:51:22.810
manufacturers as a grade B product. Windmill towers topped by their flower-like fans are a

00:51:22.810 --> 00:51:29.890
common sight on most Amish farms. Windmills pump water into storage reservoirs. These

00:51:30.060 --> 00:51:37.470
tanks are usually situated in the house's attic, the barn's loft, or on higher elevated land.

00:52:18.170 --> 00:52:23.070
If you journey to Ohio's Amish country, I highly recommend spending more than just one day.

00:52:23.740 --> 00:52:27.600
There are hundreds of miles of scenic back roads waiting to be explored.

00:52:28.390 --> 00:52:29.970
This area is rich with

00:52:30.060 --> 00:52:36.250
quality bed and breakfasts and unique inns. If you really want to meet and talk with the Amish,

00:52:36.520 --> 00:52:43.020
you might wish to stay at one of their fine bed and breakfasts. These B&Bs are reasonably priced

00:52:43.020 --> 00:52:49.620
and will quickly become your home away from home. This bed and breakfast is owned by Dale Schlebaugh,

00:52:49.840 --> 00:52:56.370
the blacksmith you saw in this video. It's one of the newest B&Bs in the Sugar Creek area

00:52:56.370 --> 00:52:59.970
and is a good representation of the country quaintness

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:14.050
and hominess of an Amish bed and breakfast. This authentic Amish farmhouse has a beautiful

00:53:14.050 --> 00:53:18.570
front porch with a fabulous view of the barn and the fields.

00:53:30.120 --> 00:53:33.420
There are two bedrooms and a center bath on the main floor.

00:53:35.240 --> 00:53:39.280
The living room is open and well-lit by the many windows.

00:53:40.160 --> 00:53:45.980
Incidentally, when the Amish build a home, windows are strategically placed for light and function,

00:53:46.000 --> 00:53:49.550
with little or no regard for exterior symmetry.

00:53:53.910 --> 00:53:59.980
Few activities inspire a sense of nostalgia than a good old-fashioned sleigh ride through the hilly...

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:07.140
valleys of Ohio's Amish countryside. Sleigh rides are available from different people or businesses

00:54:07.140 --> 00:54:14.330
at different times. I hitched my ride at the Guggisburg Swiss Inn in Charm. Having an Amish

00:54:14.330 --> 00:54:19.930
driver with a couple of his well-trained Belgians just adds to the flavor and fun of this experience.

00:54:30.030 --> 00:54:34.980
Wintertime in Amish country has its own unique flavor that many overlook.

00:54:35.900 --> 00:54:39.880
Winter scenery here is as beautiful as anywhere else in America.

00:56:02.200 --> 00:56:09.290
Oh yeah, I like it better at night. Oh yeah, it's more fun, especially when the moon is bright.

00:56:46.540 --> 00:56:52.060
have all sang the lyrics dashing through the snow in a one-horse open sleigh at some point in our

00:56:52.060 --> 00:56:57.770
lives. If you want to really know the fun and thrill that that feels like you'll have to make

00:56:57.770 --> 00:56:59.970
the trip to Ohio's Amish country when there's

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:05.650
snow on the ground and ask around. The locals know who to call or ask to put

00:57:05.650 --> 00:57:08.410
you in touch with somebody who's offering sleigh rides.

